Jim Copeland (jcopelan@nyx10.cs.du.edu) wrote:
>
>: Who else out there also enjoys having a couple of strong-arm buddies along
>: to soften up those big nasties?  I take great delight in trying to get a
>: nice little army to go along with me on my escapades.  Any other tales
>: involving fun with pets?  What are some of your favorite/unique
>: combinations of/strangest pets? 

Pets are great fun. Charm Monster is my favorite spell.
You don't like the tedium of the maze-like mines? No problem. Get a
pet Umber Hulk. The mines are non-existant in no time.
Tired of the monsters drinking their extrahealing/gain level potions
or reading those scrolls before you can kill them? No problem. Get a
pet nymph or succubus. The steal them all from them before they can
use them. Had a pet succubus who cleaned out all the guards in Gnome
town by systematically stealing their weapons and armour, then hacking
them to bits. =)
Find you  get killed by the WoY summoning 10 bazillion nasty monsters
around you at one time? Just cast a Charm Monster, and let them beat
up on each other... then take those that remain tame off to kill
a few more things. (gotta love when the wiz gets swallowed and digested
by your newly aquired pet trapper)
(oh.. and having tame monsters around you also lets you get out of the
heat as well, as you can 'exchange' places with the tame ones to get
out of the center of the conflict) 
Pet chameleons are always good for a few laughs. And a pet purple
worm is just plain nasty. A pet long worm is fun for a level, but
you usually won't be able to get him down the stairs after that.
Pet Master Lichs are cool, cause they teleport around. Had one
'port into the castle, grab the WoW and 'port back out with it. Was
the first time I never had to do the castle. Just avoided the whole
thing. Cockatrices are fun, if you have a pickaxe.
And many ofthem are just plain nasty... dragons, jabberwocks, various
demons, et al.

Whatever your pet, zap it with a wand of speed, and a wand of invisibility
(or get the intelligent ones to pick up an invis potions and drink it).
This makes them much more a killing force. (though it is good (and a safe)
practice to make sure you can see invisible before making your pet invis)

Even the imobile monsters are handy. Had a pet blue jelly that saved
my bacon on a number of occassions. Of course, you need a magic whistle
to make this an effective method. (I LOVE magic whistles!)

If you have magic resistance (via cloak/GDSM/magicbane) then getting
a pet you can live with is simply a matter of finding a polymorph
trap. Then just stand on it, and exchange places with your pet when
he's beside you, thus forcing him onto the trap. After a few times,
he will eventually be something interesting.

And nothing better then a pet to clean up all those soldier corpses =)

